# 11 — Distribution

> **For the agent reading this:** Read `plans/08-semantics-and-entities` and `plans/09-review-loop` first (the full tool suite, semantics, shots, the Walk tool, and MCP review loop). Phase 10 is the array tool (handled concurrently). This phase takes Orlablocks from a developer repository that requires `git clone` and `npm run dev` to a distributed, standalone product that anyone (level designers, indie devs, game artists) can download and use with zero dev tools. It adds:
> - **a production build:** decoupling `src/web` from the Vite dev server into optimized static assets served directly by Express;
> - **a lightweight Control Panel desktop app (No Electron):** a visible, clean desktop window (via Tauri 2.0) that manages the background server, lets users choose their **Data folder**, provides one-click launch to their default browser, and exposes all agent integrations;
> - **zero-touch MCP agent configuration:** one-click copy and auto-installer for Claude Desktop, Claude Code, Antigravity, Cursor, and Windsurf;
> - **the Orlablocks Skill (`SKILL.md`):** packaging what is currently injected via `CLAUDE.md` / `AGENTS.md` into a portable, standard agent skill that any agent can activate when designing levels;
> - **packaged releases:** standalone macOS `.app` / `.dmg` (and Windows installer) that run with zero prerequisite software (no Node.js, no npm).
>
> The work is split into small increments (§6). Each one keeps the human ↔ agent loop working. Add this phase's terms to `GLOSSARY.md` (marked "from 11") as they land. Log progress in §8 at the end of this file.

