## 2. Scope

### In

- **Production static build (11.1):**
  - Vite production build for `src/web` outputting to `dist/web/` (HTML, minified bundle, CSS, `manifold-3d` wasm);
  - Express server static file middleware (`express.static`) serving `dist/web/` in production mode;
  - graceful fallback: runs Vite middleware in dev (`NODE_ENV !== "production"`), serves static assets in production;
  - health-check endpoint (`GET /api/health`) returning server status, port, open project/scene, and active data folder.
- **Server standalone packaging (11.2):**
  - bundle server runtime with Node SEA (Single Executable Application) or Tauri sidecar embedding Node runtime;
  - dynamic port allocation with fallback (checks 5170, falls back to 5171..5175 if occupied);
  - configurable `DATA_DIR` passed via CLI flag (`--data <path>`) or environment variable;
  - clean process management (starts on app launch, terminates on window close/quit).
- **Control Panel Desktop GUI (11.3):**
  - built with **Tauri 2.0** (Rust + lightweight native webview, ~15MB binary, no Chromium/Electron);
  - dedicated visible desktop window (560 × 640 px) with tabs/sections:
    - **Dashboard Tab:**
      - Server Status indicator (Running / Stopped / Error), active port, and process health;
      - Prominent **"Open Editor in Browser"** primary action button;
      - Data Folder section: current directory path, "Change..." native directory picker (`NSOpenPanel` on macOS / File Dialog on Windows), "Open in Finder" button, and recent folders dropdown;
      - Server restart / stop button.
    - **Agents & MCP Tab:**
      - Cards for Claude Desktop, Claude Code, Antigravity, Cursor, and Windsurf;
      - Live connection status check for `http://127.0.0.1:<port>/mcp`;
      - One-click copy buttons for config snippets and terminal commands;
      - One-click auto-installer for Claude Desktop (`claude_desktop_config.json`).
    - **Skill & Instructions Tab:**
      - One-click "Install Skill" to Antigravity (`~/.gemini/antigravity/skills/orlablocks/SKILL.md`) or Claude;
      - "Export to Project" button to drop `SKILL.md` or a markdown instructions block into any game folder.
- **The Orlablocks Agent Skill (11.4):**
  - a self-contained `SKILL.md` following standard agent skill format:
    - YAML frontmatter (name: `orlablocks`, description, tags);
    - concise instructions covering world units (meters, north = -z), shapes, holes, ramps, notes, entities, and undo semantics;
    - prompt templates and common workflows (creating rooms, cutting doors, placing entity prefabs, checking sightlines with shots);
  - MCP prompts and resource endpoints: server advertises `orlablocks://guide/core` and `orlablocks://guide/design` as standard MCP resources.
- **Distribution & Installers (11.5):**
  - macOS release: signed `.dmg` containing `Orlablocks.app` (Universal binary: Apple Silicon + Intel);
  - Windows release: standalone `.zip` and lightweight installer;
  - automatic update check or release notification in the Control Panel.

### Out (deliberately deferred or dropped)

- **Menu-bar / System tray daemon:** Dropped in favor of a standard visible desktop window UI that opens on launch and quits on close.
- **Electron wrapper:** Electron adds ~150-200MB bundle size, duplicate RAM usage, and separates the editor from the user's preferred browser profile. The lightweight Control Panel + default system browser architecture gives a 10x smaller footprint and better 3D performance.
- **Cloud hosting / SaaS:** Orlablocks remains 100% local-first and private. Your data stays on your machine.
- **In-editor chat / agent runner:** Orlablocks does not embed an LLM runner inside the editor. Agents remain external (Claude, Cursor, Antigravity) connecting through the standard MCP protocol.
- **Multi-user collaborative editing:** Real-time multi-human editing on the same scene. One human + one agent remains the design target.

